save('presentation.html',f'<!doctype html><html lang="zh-Hant"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>讀懂波斯地毯紋樣 · 教學簡報</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"></head><body><header><a class="brand" href="index.html">Persian Rug Motifs</a><a href="index.html">英文 Wiki</a><a href="sources.html">來源</a><a href="checking-log.html">檢查紀錄</a></header><div class="progress" id="progress"></div><div id="content">{deck}</div>{nav}<script src="slides.js"></script></body></html>')
save('slides.js','''(()=>{const slides=[...document.querySelectorAll('.slide')],sel=document.getElementById('jump');let n=0;function show(i){n=Math.max(0,Math.min(slides.length-1,i));slides.forEach((s,k)=>{s.classList.toggle('active',k===n);s.inert=k!==n});sel.value=n;document.getElementById('prev').disabled=n===0;document.getElementById('next').disabled=n===slides.length-1;document.getElementById('counter').textContent=`${n+1}/18`;document.getElementById('progress').style.width=`${(n+1)/18*100}%`;history.replaceState(null,'',`#slide-${n+1}`);window.scrollTo(0,0)}document.getElementById('prev').onclick=()=>show(n-1);document.getElementById('next').onclick=()=>show(n+1);sel.onchange=()=>show(Number(sel.value));document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(['SELECT','INPUT','TEXTAREA','SUMMARY','BUTTON','A'].includes(e.target.tagName))return;if(e.key==='ArrowRight'){e.preventDefault();show(n+1)}if(e.key==='ArrowLeft'){e.preventDefault();show(n-1)}if(e.key==='Home')show(0);if(e.key==='End')show(slides.length-1)});const read=()=>show((Number(location.hash.match(/slide-(\\d+)/)?.[1])||1)-1);window.addEventListener('hashchange',read);read()})();''')

log='''<h1>Actual execution and checking log</h1><p>Run date: 24 November 2026 (Asia/Taipei). Research and authorship were AI-assisted. This log separates source review, structural tests and browser observations.</p><h2>Research and editorial checks</h2><table><thead><tr><th>ID / node</th><th>Observed issue</th><th>Action and status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>R01 / source screening</td><td>Met Five Medallion Carpet, object 452100, is Egyptian Mamluk, not Persian.</td><td>Rejected as a Persian example. Attribution check moved before image selection.</td></tr><tr><td>R02 / date reconciliation</td><td>Iranica IV cites Ardabil as 1535–36; the current V&A essay says 1539–1540.</td><td>Use current holding-museum record; flag the discrepancy in S01. Do not silently merge dates.</td></tr><tr><td>R03 / terminology</td><td>Shah Abbasi is also a pattern term, while the proposed topic calls it a palmette.</td><td>Retain the requested heading with an explicit distinction. Do not label every palmette Shah Abbasi.</td></tr><tr><td>R04 / image permission</td><td>V&A article is publicly readable but images are copyright-labelled.</td><td>Link only. Embed two independently verified Met public-domain images.</td></tr><tr><td>R05 / source access</td><td>Royal Collection full-page retrieval failed; institutional description was available through search.</td><td>Ingest only the visible description and disclose its limited access in S09. Nine other full records satisfy the source minimum.</td></tr><tr><td>R06 / acquisition tooling</td><td>Default local network request failed.</td><td>Public Met API/image retrieval succeeded through approved network execution. No API key used.</td></tr><tr><td>R07 / translation</td><td>No human Chinese reviewer supplied.</td><td>Chinese explicitly unreviewed. Descriptive names are provisional, not standardized museum terms.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Reproducible structural check</h2><p>Run <code>python scripts/build.py</code>, then <code>python scripts/check.py</code>. The checker validates links and fragment IDs, evidence references, minimum sources, slide count and image files. It cannot certify art-historical accuracy.</p><p><a href="data/check-results.json">Machine-readable actual results</a></p><div id="checksummary">CHECK_SUMMARY</div><h2>Browser review</h2><div>BROWSER_RESULTS</div><h2>Reflection</h2><p>The source-to-claim step needed the most editorial attention in this run: attribution, conflicting dates and naming scope. This is a qualitative observation from one run, not a measured long-term failure rate. Source screening now precedes illustration selection and translation. The process remains a loop because a slide wording problem must be corrected in the Wiki, not only on the slide.</p><p>Image permission review also became an early gate. A public article alone is insufficient permission to copy its photographs. Remaining limits: Chinese human review, no specialist authentication of unknown rugs, and no quantitative valuation model.</p><h2>Evidence of process</h2><p>The user selected the topic, supplied scope and language rules, excluded personal photos, and approved the 15-slide plus 3-appendix outline. These are actual decisions in this chat. No synthetic conversation screenshot or fabricated execution result is included.</p>'''
